        "The source positions the final two ideas as the top of a product ladder. Smaller products help customers build trust. Some customers then discover a larger problem that requires a deeper, more personalised solution.\nIdea 34 — Sell the result, not a pile of content\nConcept: Build a premium offer around a meaningful transformation rather than adding more videos, modules, and bonuses.",
        "The transcript's example is a 90-day programme called “Rate Escape,” intended to help freelancers move away from low hourly rates and toward productised services. It describes live calls and a custom plan, with a speaker-proposed price of $5,000.",
